  "staticCausalReview": [
    "The original constructor exclusively creates an empty file and enqueues the header. It does not acknowledge durable header bytes before returning.",
    "The original worker can legitimately write the header between two read_bytes calls. The remote b-empty versus header first failure matches this scheduling gap.",
    "A duplicate constructor checks lexists for source and guards before creating/opening any writer file; its FileExistsError remains required and unchanged.",
    "The added public flush waits for the accepted header target and explicit generation to become durable; no subsequent append is issued before byte equality.",
    "The scheduler fixture releases only the original worker through public flush and still invokes the real duplicate constructor. It retains FileExistsError and byte-equality assertions and does not suppress write exceptions. It is a separately labeled scheduling demonstration, not a new product guarantee."
  ],
  "scope": "Independent original-source snapshot plus one public test barrier, original 21 cases rerun once on local files; no remote CI rerun, full product suite, database or performance acceptance claim.",
